p-to-searchparameter-derived-indexes","content":"Relationship to SearchParameter derived indexes","locale":"en"},"234":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-9","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#with-nodejs","content":"You will see console printing the information below:","locale":"en"},"235":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-10","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#with-docker-compose","content":"The example of `docker-compose.yaml` file in root path","locale":"en"},"236":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-11","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#mongodb-schema-and-index-provisioning","content":"Burni sets Mongoose `autoCreate` and `autoIndex` to `false` by default. Model registration only means models are registered inside the application process; it does **not** guarantee that MongoDB collections or indexes exist. Production deployments should run provisioning before application startup, or explicitly enable startup opt-in.","locale":"en"},"237":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-12","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#mongodb-schema-and-index-provisioning","content":"The desired collection and index manifest is generated deterministically at runtime from registered models, the model catalog, approved built-in temporal definitions, and non-temporal SearchParameter derived indexes that pass policy. The manifest stores `artifactIdentity` (compiled SearchParameter artifact) and `derivedIndexPolicy.searchParameterPolicyVersion` (non-temporal index policy). Provisioning reconciles MongoDB against that generated manifest, persists results in `MongoProvisioningState`, and uses `MongoProvisioningLock` with a database-scoped lease for multi-instance runs. Use `writeDesiredManifestArtifact()` when you need a persisted JSON copy (default path `models/mongodb/provisioning/artifacts/desired-index-manifest.json`).","locale":"en"},"238":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-13","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#pre-deployment-provisioning-recommended","content":"Configure the same MongoDB connection environment variables as the application (`MONGODB_CONNECTION_URL`, or `MONGODB_HOSTS` / `MONGODB_PORTS` / `MONGODB_NAME`), then run:","locale":"en"},"239":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-14","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#pre-deployment-provisioning-recommended","content":"This command runs control-plane initialization, acquires the lock, creates collections, creates baseline indexes, creates approved built-in derived indexes (temporal and non-temporal SearchParameters), runs verify, and persists the manifest checksum and drift summary. Exit code `0` on success; any failed phase returns a non-zero status.","locale":"en"},"240":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-15","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#pre-deployment-provisioning-recommended","content":"**Partial completion and retry**: Provisioning is additive-only and does not roll back collections or indexes that were already created. If a run fails midway, completed DDL remains in place; rerunning `mongodb:provision` continues from the desired/actual diff. After lock lease expiry, another process can reclaim the expired lock and retry.","locale":"en"},"241":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-16","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#read-only-verify","content":"`mongodb:verify` performs **no DDL** and does not modify data. It reads actual collections and indexes and reports:","locale":"en"},"242":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-17","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#read-only-verify","content":"**missing**: indexes expected by the manifest but absent in the database","locale":"en"},"243":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-18","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#read-only-verify","content":"**extra**: indexes present in the database but not declared in the manifest (reported only, never deleted)","locale":"en"},"244":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-19","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#read-only-verify","content":"**mismatch**: indexes whose key or options do not match the expected identity","locale":"en"},"245":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-20","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#read-only-verify","content":"**manifest identity drift**: the current desired manifest checksum or version differs from the value stored in `MongoProvisioningState` for the latest successful run","locale":"en"},"246":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-21","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#read-only-verify","content":"Verify failure uses exit code `2`.","locale":"en"},"247":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-22","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#id-duplicate-audit-read-only","content":"Scans resource and history collections for duplicate `id` values for a future unique-migration clean-audit gate. It **does not modify data**. General provisioning does **not** automatically change an existing `id` index to unique.","locale":"en"},"248":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-23","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#startup-opt-in","content":"By default, `node server.js` does **not** run provisioning. Application readiness (`mongodb.ready`) and provisioning readiness are separate. Missing performance indexes (including non-temporal derived indexes) do not block HTTP listen, but queries may fall back to COLLSCAN; `mongodb:verify` diagnostics report missing performance indexes.","locale":"en"},"249":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-24","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#startup-opt-in","content":"To wait for a full provisioning run before application ready, set:","locale":"en"},"250":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-25","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#startup-opt-in","content":"or `MONGODB_PROVISION_ON_STARTUP=1`. When enabled, server bootstrap runs the same locked run as `mongodb:provision` before listen. On failure it does not declare ready, does not listen, and exits with a non-zero status. Production deployments should still prefer the standalone deployment command over startup opt-in.","locale":"en"},"251":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy-26","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/deploy#relationship-to-searchparameter-derived-indexes","content":"The derived index manifest merges temporal and policy-approved non-temporal built-in lookups (token, reference, string, number, quantity, uri). Custom database SearchParameters remain executable but do not create derived indexes by default. Derived index reconcile is additive-only: missing indexes can be created by `provision`, while extra or mismatched indexes are reported by `verify` and never auto-deleted; query runtime does not use `$hint`. Rollback can disable the new policy or restore a manifest version without auto-deleting indexes already created. See Search parameters overview and ADR 0010.","locale":"en"},"252":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","type":"page","content":"Installation","breadcrumbs":["Docs","v2 (LTS)","Getting Started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","locale":"en"},"253":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation-0","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation#with-git","content":"With git","locale":"en"},"254":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation-1","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","content":"Please confirm that you have the:","locale":"en"},"255":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation-2","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","content":"git","locale":"en"},"256":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation-3","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","content":"Node.js >= 22","locale":"en"},"257":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation-4","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","content":"MongoDB > 4.2","locale":"en"},"258":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation-5","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation#with-git","content":"Clone from git","locale":"en"},"259":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation-6","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation#with-git","content":"Install dependencies","locale":"en"},"260":{"id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation-7","page_id":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/getting-started/installation#with-git","content":"after installation, let's starting configuration","locale":"en"},"261":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","type":"page","content":"Add search parameter","breadcrumbs":["Docs","v2 (LTS)","Search Parameters"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","locale":"en"},"262":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-0","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#example-bundlecomposition-and-bundlemessage","content":"Example: Bundle.composition and Bundle.message","locale":"en"},"263":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-1","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#direct-identity-search","content":"Direct identity search","locale":"en"},"264":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-2","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#chained-search","content":"Chained search","locale":"en"},"265":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-3","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#limitations","content":"Limitations","locale":"en"},"266":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-4","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","content":"The code about search parameters can be found in `models\\FHIR\\queryBuild.js` and `models\\FHIR\\searchParameterQueryHandler.js` files.","locale":"en"},"267":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-5","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","content":"`queryBuild.js`: get single MongoDB query object from data type.","locale":"en"},"268":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-6","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","content":"`searchParameterQueryHandler.js`: using `queryBuild.js` and get fully MongoDB query object from HTTP query param.","locale":"en"},"269":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-7","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","content":"Some search parameters from generator will got missing or incorrect. You can fix by using methods in `models\\FHIR\\searchParameterQueryHandler.js`.","locale":"en"},"270":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-8","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#example-bundlecomposition-and-bundlemessage","content":"FHIR R4 defines `Bundle.composition` and `Bundle.message` as reference search parameters. Burni resolves them from the SearchParameter Registry and evaluates only `entry[0].resource`:","locale":"en"},"271":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-9","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#example-bundlecomposition-and-bundlemessage","content":"`composition` — `document` Bundles whose first entry is a `Composition`","locale":"en"},"272":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-10","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#example-bundlecomposition-and-bundlemessage","content":"`message` — `message` Bundles whose first entry is a `MessageHeader`","locale":"en"},"273":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-11","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#example-bundlecomposition-and-bundlemessage","content":"Burni does not fan out across all `entry` elements. Only the first embedded resource participates in these special searches.","locale":"en"},"274":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-12","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#direct-identity-search","content":"Supported value forms include relative `ResourceType/id`, a bare id normalized to the fixed target type, and an absolute URL that matches `entry[0].fullUrl`. Versioned, contained, and logical identifier references are rejected.","locale":"en"},"275":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-13","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#direct-identity-search","content":"Example URLs:","locale":"en"},"276":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-14","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#chained-search","content":"After the inline hop, Burni applies the target resource SearchParameter plan from the Registry. Examples:","locale":"en"},"277":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-15","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#chained-search","content":"`composition.patient` follows `Composition::patient` and may fan out to `Patient` and `Group`. `MessageHeader.focus` is an open reference target, so a type filter is required before chaining further:","locale":"en"},"278":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-16","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#chained-search","content":"This request is rejected with HTTP 400 and `missing-type-filter`.","locale":"en"},"279":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-17","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#limitations","content":"Only `entry[0].resource` is evaluated; later entries do not affect results even when they contain a matching Composition or MessageHeader.","locale":"en"},"280":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter-18","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/add-search-parameter#limitations","content":"Bundle type and first-entry resource type must match; invalid stored Bundles simply do not match rather than returning parameter errors.","locale":"en"},"281":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","type":"page","content":"Overview","breadcrumbs":["Docs","v2 (LTS)","Search Parameters"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","locale":"en"},"282":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-0","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#search-parameters-overview","content":"Search parameters overview","locale":"en"},"283":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-1","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#search-parameter-types","content":"Search Parameter Types","locale":"en"},"284":{"id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview-2","page_id":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/v2/search-parameter/overview#parameters-for-all